"source_slot": 1,
"patient_paragraph": 1,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "unconditional_excluded",
"comment": "The guideline states a person is not fit for an unconditional licence if BP is consistently >170 systolic or >100 diastolic. The nurse note records a single reading of 172/98 mmHg taken after the patient hurried up the stairs, with no repeat measurement and no evidence of consistency over time."
},
{
"source_slot": 3,
"patient_paragraph": 1,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "conditional_qualified",
"comment": "The guideline requires effective control over a 4-week follow-up period and absence of driving-impairing side effects. The nurse note indicates the patient recently changed tablets and feels briefly light-headed when rising, but does not confirm whether this constitutes a driving-impairing side effect or if control has been achieved over the required 4-week period."
},
{
"source_slot": 3,
"patient_paragraph": 1,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "conditional_qualified",
"comment": "The guideline requires information from a treating specialist regarding effective control and side effects. The nurse note mentions the patient recently changed tablets but does not provide a report or opinion from a specialist confirming treatment stability."
},
{
"source_slot": 4,
"patient_paragraph": 1,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "conditional_qualified",
"comment": "The guideline states that the initial recommendation of a conditional licence must be based on the opinion of an appropriate medical specialist. The nurse note does not contain a specialist's opinion."
},
{
"source_slot": 1,
"patient_paragraph": 2,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "conditional_qualified",
"comment": "The guideline requires assessment of side effects impairing safe driving. The nurse note reports the patient says headlights split into two after several hours at night, but notes the effect disappeared before examination and that the patient cannot say whether covering one eye changes it."
},
{
"source_slot": 1,
"patient_paragraph": 2,
"applicability": "unresolved",
"finding": "conditional_qualified",
"comment": "The guideline requires assessment of evidence of damage to target organs relevant to driving. The nurse note mentions a six-month-old slip with 6/9 and 6/12 vision but explicitly states no current acuity or specialist report is available."
}
],
"fitness": "undetermined",
"outcome": "insufficient_information",
"explanation": "The assessment cannot determine if the patient meets unconditional standards because there is insufficient evidence to establish that blood pressure is 'consistently' above the exclusion threshold; the recorded reading was a single event following physical exertion without repeat measurements. The assessment also cannot determine if the patient may meet conditional standards because critical prerequisites are missing: there is no specialist opinion confirming effective control over a 4-week period, no confirmation of absence of driving-impairing side effects (the reported photopsia and light-headedness require clarification regarding severity and persistence), and no evidence to rule out damage to target organs. The nurse note explicitly states that treatment stability, persistent pressure confirmation, and specialist information remain to be clarified.","missing_information": ["Consistent blood pressure readings over time to confirm exclusion criteria or conditional control", "Specialist opinion confirming effective hypertension control over a 4-week period", "Confirmation that light-headedness upon rising is not driving-impairing", "Evidence of absence of damage to target organs relevant to driving", "Current visual acuity and specialist report regarding night vision symptoms"]}
